CompTIA Security+ (Exam SYO-501)


1  Identifying Security Fundamentals
---------------------------------------------------
Learning Outcomes
Having completed this module you will be able to:
Discuss identifying security fundamentals.
List the goals of information security.
Define risk and recognise vulnerabilities in information security.
Explain how the concept of information security works together to provide computer security.
Underline the three principles of security control and management.
Compare passwords, tokens, biometrics, geolocation and other forms of authentication.
Identify basic cryptography concepts.


Lesson Summary
Identifying security fundamentals includes information security concepts, basic security controls, basic authentication and authorization concepts, and cryptography concepts.
Vulnerabilities in information refer to improperly configured or installed hardware and software, delays in applying and testing software and firmware patches, unlisted software and firmware patches, bugs in software or OS, poor physical security, insecure passwords, among others.
Three principles of security control and management are confidentiality, integrity and availability.
User name and password combination is a widely used authentication scheme. Other methods of authentication are tokens, biometrics, geolocation, as well as a keystroke, multi-factor and mutual authentications.
Cryptography is the science of hiding information, most commonly by encoding and decoding a secret code used to sent messages.


